tting here provides little value as you are unlikely to be called by worse hands (worse high cards) and may fold out hands you are currently beating or splitting with, while risking a check-raise if the opponent has a 4 or a set. Checking back allows you to see the River for free, giving you a chance to pair your King or Ten, or win at showdown with King High if the opponent is also on a missed high-card hand.\n\nReason: The pot is small, and the board texture is dangerous with straight possibilities. Checking is the safest play to realize equity and avoid bloating the pot with a marginal hand that has showdown value against bluffs or weaker high cards.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
